  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">University of the South Pacific Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia has been a long time supporter of the University of the South Pacific (USP), which is an important provider of graduates for community, industry and government in the region. USP provides a critical workforce for economic development, particularly in areas of new technology and responding to challenges such as climate change, natural disasters, renewable energy, and oceans, which are important to Australia&apos;s interests. The partnership provides flexible funding to support implementation of USP&apos;s Strategic Plan, which aims to meet the tertiary education needs of the Pacific. The partnership also supports the Pacific to implement the Pacific Education Regional Framework (PacREF), with a focus on improving the quality of teacher education in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
